\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(3x+y)\\,dx+x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+4t-1)\\cdot 2t+{t}^{2}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2}-2t+4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}+4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{4}+4(2)^{3}-{2}^{2}]-[0] \\\\  & =[24+32-4] \\\\  & =52\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz,$ where $C$ is a portion of the line $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,4]?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c8aeb24-90cc-5de9-a270-6cd27812a200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413043 #edb/ref 1074 "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\sqrt{2}t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,z(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx+{z}^{3}\\,dy-{y}^{2}\\,dz & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+{z}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})+8{t}^{3}\\cdot (2)-4{t}^{2}\\cdot (2)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}16{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
